WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:33.249 --> 00:00:36.130
I love to play with human bodies

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.169
because everyone can connect with it.

00:00:39.169 --> 00:00:41.303
Everyone is a human, basically.

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:50.070
People come to me saying
that they like the way

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.700
I'm thinking because the clip is

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.231
a little bit different,
so not too obvious.

00:00:56.231 --> 00:00:57.841
You really have to think when you see it.

00:00:57.841 --> 00:01:01.508
You really have to think,
"What does it mean?"

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:07.330
I'm trying to hide the
obvious, so not like...

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.830
because when you go today on
the social media channels,

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.780
you scroll down and everything is like

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:13.913
seen a thousand times.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:20.980
It's somehow disgusting,
but with the colors

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:23.380
and everything it's nothing.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.560
That's why I'm using also
these really light monotone

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.780
colors because frankly,
if I would use dark stuff,

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.700
everyone would say this is
disgusting, this is s---,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:34.867
and I don't wanna watch it.

00:01:40.982 --> 00:01:43.550
It was basically to learn the 3D program,

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:47.040
which I'm working on
mostly, and this 3D program

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.507
is really good for simulations and VFX,

00:01:50.507 --> 00:01:53.360
and I had a really big motivation, like,

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.543
I was also coming home
after my working hours,

00:01:57.543 --> 00:01:59.620
grabbing my iPad, and I was watching

00:01:59.620 --> 00:02:03.800
three or four hours of tutorials
just to learn something.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.060
When I started, every
clip was like a challenge

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:11.060
in terms of technical set-up,
and I realized really fast

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.453
that it's more than just a technical test.

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.010
And now it's basically like an

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.690
art and a business at the same time.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.810
When I'm posting something there are tons

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:37.640
of comments and reshares automatically.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.610
It's crazy. I can just wait.

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:42.970
If I post something, I can
wait, the next two days

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.363
I'm getting job requests
also from big companies.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:53.190
It's really important in 3D
that you know what you're doing

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:55.590
before you start because, as I said,

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.810
simulations are really time-consuming,

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.339
so for a five-second
clip you sometimes need

00:03:01.339 --> 00:03:03.000
three or four days to get it perfectly

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:06.480
because simulations are
really hard to art direct,

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.090
and it's more a little bit luck

00:03:08.090 --> 00:03:09.690
and experience at the same time.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:15.370
For me it's like a game, a puzzle,

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:18.273
this program, it's fun
and work at the same time.

